:: Define Projects [system] {"position":"1125,0","size":"100,100"}
/* Projects ====================================================================
   $company.projects: every job the company can take on, story ones and repeatable ones. The CMD Projects
   panel lists the active ones; the Project Overview dialog (the arrow in that panel) lists all of them.
   Every project is started by the player in the overview, never by the story: mails, quests and other
   projects only unlock them (setup.unlockProject).

   id               string, project_<client>_<what>. Look a project up with setup.getProjectById(id)
   title            may contain variables
   description      one or two sentences for the overview, may contain variables
   type             "story": done once, the story waits for it. "repeatable": can be taken on again after
                    it was finished (after cooldown days)
   unlocked         false: a future project. The overview hides it and it can not start, so nothing gets
                    spoiled. The story reveals it with setup.unlockProject(id): in a quest set (best place),
                    a mail answer eval or the onComplete of another project. Leave it out for projects the
                    player can start from the beginning
   unlock           optional TwineScript strings, all have to be true before it can start. Only for projects
                    the player already knows about: the overview shows them as Locked with this list
   unlockText       the same conditions, readable, in the same order
   cooldown         repeatable only, days after finishing before it can be started again (default 0)
   duration         days until it is due, counted from the start
   task             id of the task that belongs to it (Define Tasks), shown in the project window.
                    onStart activates it
   revenue          paid every night while it is active
   reward           paid once on completion (shrinks when late, see "Project logic" below). 0 for an in-house
                    project nobody pays for
   outcome          what an in-house project (reward 0) gives instead, shown where the reward would be
   requirements     work needed per skill category. 0 means the skill is not needed
   client           copy of the client NPC (read the live one through State.variables[client.sysName]).
                    Leave it out for an in-house project
   location         copy of the location it happens at
   staff            optional list of the sysNames who may work on it (["brian"]): the project window only offers
                    them, and nobody else's work counts. Without it everyone may (setup.projectAllows)

   Set while playing: active, startedAtDay, due, completed (the last run is finished), completedAtDay,
   timesCompleted, assigned (employee copies), progress, seenRun (see "New projects" below). */
<<set $company.projects to [
	{
